1
00:01:09,410 --> 00:01:14,740
[Connecting to You]

2
00:01:24,680 --> 00:01:30,100
[The 4th Thread] [Personal Distance]

3
00:01:30,120 --> 00:01:36,160
[Redefining Your Relationship by Distance]

4
00:01:37,160 --> 00:01:38,039
Wow.

5
00:01:38,539 --> 00:01:41,289
Doesn't this guy know what fresh food is?

6
00:01:43,950 --> 00:01:45,160
Hey.

7
00:01:45,789 --> 00:01:47,910
Lin Jiakai.

8
00:01:48,910 --> 00:01:50,289
What's wrong?

9
00:01:53,910 --> 00:01:57,039
Could you please
bring me some toilet paper?

10
00:01:57,539 --> 00:02:00,450
Toilet paper? Where is it?

11
00:02:00,760 --> 00:02:05,450
It's on a shelf in the tatami room.

12
00:02:14,450 --> 00:02:15,540
Is it there?

13
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:29,040
New roommate, hope we get along well.

14
00:02:30,660 --> 00:02:32,410
Hope we get along well.

15
00:02:36,079 --> 00:02:37,579
I won't stay long.

16
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:40,600
I'll move back in 2 months at most.

17
00:02:41,040 --> 00:02:41,910
Okay.

18
00:02:42,450 --> 00:02:44,579
Please let me finish
using the toilet first.

19
00:02:44,579 --> 00:02:46,829
Sorry, take your time.

20
00:02:56,680 --> 00:02:59,740
-This is really good. Want a bite?
-You, you... this...

21
00:03:01,330 --> 00:03:02,500
Here. Come here.

22
00:03:02,530 --> 00:03:04,040
Don't drop crumbs. Don't.

23
00:03:04,040 --> 00:03:04,450
Get up. Get up.

24
00:03:04,450 --> 00:03:05,330
Get up. Get up.

25
00:03:05,830 --> 00:03:08,450
You really are...
Let me hold this, and you hold this.

26
00:03:08,450 --> 00:03:10,700
Don't drop crumbs. Eat over this.

27
00:03:10,700 --> 00:03:12,180
Be careful.

28
00:03:13,160 --> 00:03:14,090
What are you doing?

29
00:03:14,090 --> 00:03:14,720
Turning on the AC.

30
00:03:14,720 --> 00:03:15,700
Wait. Wait.

31
00:03:18,040 --> 00:03:19,300
Wipe your hands clean.

32
00:03:20,079 --> 00:03:20,950
Is this okay?

33
00:03:20,950 --> 00:03:22,880
Never mind, I'll turn it on for you.

34
00:03:23,079 --> 00:03:25,290
I want the AC on at 24°C.

35
00:03:25,320 --> 00:03:26,660
For an hour.

36
00:03:26,660 --> 00:03:27,790
Only for an hour?

37
00:03:27,790 --> 00:03:29,829
Right, give it to me.

38
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:33,120
My egg roll.

39
00:03:33,120 --> 00:03:34,120
It's gone.

40
00:03:36,079 --> 00:03:37,579
So many rules.

41
00:03:41,700 --> 00:03:44,579
I tell you, that cop isn't just skeptical;

42
00:03:44,579 --> 00:03:46,140
he's a total neat freak.

43
00:03:46,370 --> 00:03:47,950
Completely different from you.

44
00:03:47,950 --> 00:03:50,329
Go ahead and scold him
if you want, but why go after me?

45
00:03:50,329 --> 00:03:51,870
I can be clean if I want to. I just...

46
00:03:51,870 --> 00:03:53,579
don't want to, okay?

47
00:03:55,120 --> 00:03:56,450
Weren't you going
to sever the thread with him?

48
00:03:56,450 --> 00:03:57,620
And you actually moved in together?

49
00:03:57,620 --> 00:03:59,200
Moved in?

50
00:03:59,200 --> 00:04:00,970
I'm just staying temporarily.

51
00:04:01,250 --> 00:04:02,830
And while I'm at it, see

52
00:04:02,830 --> 00:04:04,750
how to sever the thread.

53
00:04:05,200 --> 00:04:06,660
So have you found out
what the color of the thread

54
00:04:06,660 --> 00:04:07,700
means?

55
00:04:07,700 --> 00:04:08,750
Not yet.

56
00:04:08,750 --> 00:04:10,000
But I just don't get

57
00:04:10,260 --> 00:04:12,800
what this has to do with Dawei and me.

58
00:04:14,030 --> 00:04:15,120
I need to go to the bathroom.

59
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:16,269
Wait for me a sec.

60
00:04:16,300 --> 00:04:17,250
Go where?

61
00:04:21,079 --> 00:04:22,470
The room is pretty clean.

62
00:04:22,470 --> 00:04:23,930
I thought you were asleep.

63
00:04:25,450 --> 00:04:27,050
There might be mosquitoes in this room,

64
00:04:27,050 --> 00:04:29,380
so I brought you some mosquito repellent.

65
00:04:30,250 --> 00:04:32,080
Thanks. Then...

66
00:04:32,100 --> 00:04:32,900
good night.

67
00:04:32,930 --> 00:04:33,630
Wait.

68
00:04:34,840 --> 00:04:36,090
Did you

69
00:04:36,110 --> 00:04:39,170
say something
about the relationship between us?

70
00:04:42,270 --> 00:04:43,690
Yeah, I...

71
00:04:43,940 --> 00:04:46,020
was just chatting with Chaonan,

72
00:04:46,050 --> 00:04:49,430
saying we used to be cop and suspect,

73
00:04:49,580 --> 00:04:52,200
and now we're suddenly roommates.

74
00:04:52,200 --> 00:04:54,580
It's quite a bizarre connection.

75
00:04:54,750 --> 00:04:55,850
Alright, that's it.

76
00:04:55,850 --> 00:04:56,500
Good night.

77
00:04:56,500 --> 00:04:57,520
Good night.

78
00:04:57,909 --> 00:04:59,159
Weren't you going to the bathroom?

79
00:04:59,159 --> 00:05:00,780
I'm not in a hurry.

80
00:05:01,800 --> 00:05:03,900
-But holding it is bad for your bladder.
-Don't worry. Don't worry.

81
00:05:03,900 --> 00:05:06,700
Thank you for the mosquito repellent.
Good night.

82
00:05:07,510 --> 00:05:08,950
Not in a hurry?

83
00:05:08,980 --> 00:05:10,600
It's about to burst out.

84
00:05:10,810 --> 00:05:14,730
[Police]

85
00:05:12,820 --> 00:05:14,820
Everyone, your attention, please.

86
00:05:14,870 --> 00:05:16,940
Let me introduce

87
00:05:16,970 --> 00:05:19,340
a new administrative student worker.

88
00:05:19,580 --> 00:05:22,160
Actually, you all know
this student worker.

89
00:05:22,450 --> 00:05:24,830
He is the one who helped
the police solve a case before,

90
00:05:24,830 --> 00:05:26,830
our brave little hero,

91
00:05:26,990 --> 00:05:28,410
Lin Jiakai.

92
00:05:30,400 --> 00:05:32,590
Clap louder, come on.

93
00:05:32,610 --> 00:05:33,400
Come on.

94
00:05:33,870 --> 00:05:36,240
Jiakai has

95
00:05:36,260 --> 00:05:37,500
a special intuition for finding people.

96
00:05:37,500 --> 00:05:41,170
I believe there must be areas
where he can assist us in solving cases.

97
00:05:41,170 --> 00:05:43,960
So I hope you can cooperate seamlessly,
okay?

98
00:05:43,990 --> 00:05:45,490
-Okay.
-Okay.

99
00:05:46,270 --> 00:05:46,820
Dawei.

100
00:05:46,840 --> 00:05:48,950
-Yes.
-You are sitting closest, so it's you.

101
00:05:48,950 --> 00:05:49,480
Me?

102
00:05:49,510 --> 00:05:50,050
Yes.

103
00:05:50,080 --> 00:05:51,700
Show him around the environment

104
00:05:51,700 --> 00:05:53,900
and take good care of him.

105
00:05:54,250 --> 00:05:55,620
Oh, okay.

106
00:05:57,330 --> 00:05:58,830
Nice to meet you.

107
00:06:01,620 --> 00:06:03,200
Nice to meet you.

108
00:06:11,450 --> 00:06:13,050
Could you please help me
take this upstairs?

109
00:06:13,050 --> 00:06:14,580
Thanks.

110
00:06:15,140 --> 00:06:16,720
Perverted College Student,

111
00:06:16,720 --> 00:06:17,830
what are you doing here?

112
00:06:17,830 --> 00:06:19,080
What is going on?

113
00:06:19,100 --> 00:06:21,100
Your Chief asked me before.

114
00:06:21,130 --> 00:06:24,280
I thought you knew,
but you're so surprised.

115
00:06:24,500 --> 00:06:25,460
I didn't know.

116
00:06:25,480 --> 00:06:27,300
And I don't think you
have any professional ability

117
00:06:27,300 --> 00:06:28,700
to work in the police station.

118
00:06:28,700 --> 00:06:30,700
Don't look at me. Keep working.

119
00:06:33,690 --> 00:06:34,730
To copy,

120
00:06:34,760 --> 00:06:36,470
you just put the paper in,

121
00:06:36,490 --> 00:06:37,760
then close the lid.

122
00:06:37,780 --> 00:06:40,270
There's a start button
you can press, and after you press it,

123
00:06:40,270 --> 00:06:42,200
you can select the number of pages
on the side.

124
00:06:42,200 --> 00:06:44,030
Do you understand?

125
00:06:46,680 --> 00:06:48,300
You have a lot of problems.

126
00:06:48,330 --> 00:06:50,020
Just an administrative student worker.

127
00:06:50,020 --> 00:06:51,400
What profession do I need?

128
00:06:51,400 --> 00:06:52,730
And you still talk back.

129
00:06:53,750 --> 00:06:55,530
Our little hero Jiakai.

130
00:06:56,020 --> 00:06:57,500
We just said you could help find people,

131
00:06:57,500 --> 00:06:59,030
and now there is someone for you to find.

132
00:06:59,030 --> 00:07:00,360
People nearby reported

133
00:07:00,370 --> 00:07:01,640
that an elderly person with dementia
was wandering around,

134
00:07:01,640 --> 00:07:02,840
unable to find the way home.

135
00:07:02,840 --> 00:07:05,310
We need to bother you for that...

136
00:07:05,530 --> 00:07:06,960
-Finding someone?
-Yes.

137
00:07:07,100 --> 00:07:07,760
I can do it.

138
00:07:07,790 --> 00:07:09,790
Okay, then I'll leave it to you.

139
00:07:09,810 --> 00:07:11,650
Dawei, I'll trouble you.

140
00:07:13,520 --> 00:07:15,980
This can be considered a profession,
right?

141
00:07:19,180 --> 00:07:19,850
Let's go.

142
00:07:22,170 --> 00:07:23,860
Walk behind me.

143
00:07:25,140 --> 00:07:26,470
Mr. Wu Dawei,

144
00:07:26,870 --> 00:07:28,650
don't be so impatient.

145
00:07:28,680 --> 00:07:30,400
I can really help.

146
00:07:31,140 --> 00:07:33,010
As long as that elder has an ID,

147
00:07:33,120 --> 00:07:35,680
we can find his information
and take him home.

148
00:07:35,780 --> 00:07:37,240
I really don't understand

149
00:07:37,620 --> 00:07:39,480
the point of me bringing you here.

150
00:07:39,810 --> 00:07:42,190
Do you really not
believe in my ability?

151
00:07:42,490 --> 00:07:45,690
I thought you believed me,
so you let me live in your house.

152
00:07:46,600 --> 00:07:49,150
Wu Dawei, you're really
looking for trouble.

153
00:07:51,150 --> 00:07:52,210
Listen carefully.

154
00:07:52,260 --> 00:07:54,550
You absolutely can't let anyone
at the station know

155
00:07:54,550 --> 00:07:55,909
that you're living at my house.

156
00:07:55,909 --> 00:07:58,030
Okay, I won't tell anyone.

157
00:07:58,159 --> 00:07:59,480
And when we go to work,

158
00:07:59,570 --> 00:08:01,140
we absolutely can't arrive
or leave together.

159
00:08:01,140 --> 00:08:03,270
We must stagger our schedules, got it?

160
00:08:04,140 --> 00:08:05,830
Is it necessary to go to such lengths?

161
00:08:05,830 --> 00:08:07,300
Don't you want to be an informant?

162
00:08:07,300 --> 00:08:10,230
An informant's primary responsibility
is secrecy.

163
00:08:10,310 --> 00:08:11,350
Can't you do that?

164
00:08:11,940 --> 00:08:14,100
So am I your informant now?

165
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:16,850
I'm just teaching you
how to keep a secret,

166
00:08:16,850 --> 00:08:18,450
Perverted College Student.

167
00:08:20,820 --> 00:08:21,520
Dawei!

168
00:08:25,270 --> 00:08:27,890
Your thread just suddenly...

169
00:08:28,120 --> 00:08:29,780
Don't talk to me
about any thread anymore.

170
00:08:29,780 --> 00:08:31,380
I don't understand or see it.

171
00:08:31,450 --> 00:08:32,700
Anyway, the secrecy thing

172
00:08:32,700 --> 00:08:33,620
is settled.

173
00:08:33,870 --> 00:08:35,530
If you can't do it,

174
00:08:35,559 --> 00:08:37,289
I'll have to ask you to move out.

175
00:08:38,320 --> 00:08:39,760
Why are you being like this?

176
00:08:39,760 --> 00:08:41,419
Just listen to me for a second.

177
00:09:00,050 --> 00:09:00,800
Hello.

178
00:09:00,840 --> 00:09:01,770
What's going on?

179
00:09:02,670 --> 00:09:03,920
Why are you panting?

180
00:09:04,540 --> 00:09:07,430
I need to make sure no one sees
me going into Wu Dawei's house.

181
00:09:07,430 --> 00:09:09,980
Doesn't this kind of situation
only happen to female stars

182
00:09:09,980 --> 00:09:11,680
when they're being followed by paparazzi?

183
00:09:11,680 --> 00:09:13,030
What, are you a best actress?

184
00:09:13,030 --> 00:09:15,330
None of your business. Why did you call?

185
00:09:15,360 --> 00:09:16,550
I was going to ask you,

186
00:09:16,550 --> 00:09:18,680
if you were going to treat
a girl to a meal,

187
00:09:18,680 --> 00:09:20,230
do you think it's better to treat her

188
00:09:20,230 --> 00:09:23,030
to Korean BBQ or pasta?

189
00:09:23,230 --> 00:09:26,110
Pasta, then. Why?

190
00:09:26,140 --> 00:09:28,250
Are you going to be a pawn again
and pay for the meal?

191
00:09:28,250 --> 00:09:31,850
You're the pawn. Everyone in your family
is just pawns. Bye-bye!

192
00:09:35,610 --> 00:09:36,480
Weirdo.

193
00:09:40,050 --> 00:09:41,980
He also likes to eat strawberries.

194
00:09:42,780 --> 00:09:43,910
What a coincidence.

195
00:09:48,490 --> 00:09:49,530
You're back.

196
00:09:49,550 --> 00:09:50,410
Yeah.

197
00:09:50,440 --> 00:09:51,900
I cooked dinner for you.

198
00:09:51,920 --> 00:09:53,370
Do you want to eat together?

199
00:09:53,370 --> 00:09:55,220
Is your cooking edible?

200
00:10:01,170 --> 00:10:02,520
Did it take you a long time?

201
00:10:02,520 --> 00:10:03,850
About an hour and a half.

202
00:10:04,450 --> 00:10:05,640
Do you want to try it?

203
00:10:07,930 --> 00:10:11,190
Chaonan had it and said it was better
than restaurant food.

204
00:10:24,990 --> 00:10:25,800
Is it good?

205
00:10:30,540 --> 00:10:31,490
It's alright.

206
00:10:33,390 --> 00:10:35,790
Then you can have this one.
I'll go get mine.

207
00:11:03,020 --> 00:11:04,350
What are you looking at?

208
00:11:04,830 --> 00:11:05,780
Just allergies.

209
00:11:07,100 --> 00:11:09,560
I just happen to have a backache.

210
00:11:14,490 --> 00:11:15,740
Then sit up here.

211
00:11:15,760 --> 00:11:16,890
Why sit on the floor?

212
00:11:31,190 --> 00:11:32,390
What's wrong?

213
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:39,620
It seems a shiny, oily insect
just passed by.

214
00:11:39,640 --> 00:11:40,630
A cockroach?

215
00:11:40,650 --> 00:11:42,380
You're afraid of cockroaches?

216
00:11:44,150 --> 00:11:44,880
It's flying!

217
00:11:46,280 --> 00:11:47,280
I'll kill it.

218
00:11:51,610 --> 00:11:52,340
It flew away.

219
00:11:56,830 --> 00:11:58,630
There's another one behind you.

220
00:11:59,680 --> 00:12:00,960
Where? Where is it?

221
00:12:03,040 --> 00:12:03,860
Just kidding.

222
00:12:14,450 --> 00:12:15,620
Go away.

223
00:12:15,750 --> 00:12:17,320
Is this how you treat

224
00:12:17,340 --> 00:12:19,730
the person who saved you
from a cockroach?

225
00:12:19,940 --> 00:12:22,940
What if there's a cockroach
in the house next time?

226
00:12:24,900 --> 00:12:26,100
Excuse me.

227
00:12:27,580 --> 00:12:28,710
That's more like it.

228
00:12:33,340 --> 00:12:35,250
Ladies and gentlemen!

229
00:12:35,250 --> 00:12:35,820
Jian.

230
00:12:35,850 --> 00:12:37,150
I'm back.

231
00:12:37,250 --> 00:12:38,080
Long time no see.

232
00:12:38,080 --> 00:12:39,870
-Long time no see, everyone.
-Long time no see.

233
00:12:39,870 --> 00:12:43,500
Cops, your dessert delivery is here.

234
00:12:43,670 --> 00:12:45,300
Glad you have a conscience.

235
00:12:45,320 --> 00:12:47,100
What are you saying?

236
00:12:47,120 --> 00:12:48,550
You still remember to visit old friends.

237
00:12:48,550 --> 00:12:50,100
You're too kind.

238
00:12:50,170 --> 00:12:52,620
Are you really transferring back
to the North District this time?

239
00:12:52,620 --> 00:12:55,290
South District is so chill.
Why make it hard on yourself?

240
00:12:55,290 --> 00:12:57,470
It's not up to me.
Just a routine rotation.

241
00:12:57,470 --> 00:12:58,870
-Hurry up and pick one.
-I've picked one.

242
00:12:58,870 --> 00:13:00,900
You said I had no conscience?
I'll show you what a conscience is.

243
00:13:00,900 --> 00:13:03,700
Senior, where are you
transferring to this time?

244
00:13:07,970 --> 00:13:10,030
Just the police station
in the next district.

245
00:13:10,030 --> 00:13:12,360
I just finished moving my stuff recently.

246
00:13:13,170 --> 00:13:13,910
I think a few days ago,

247
00:13:13,910 --> 00:13:15,370
at the convenience store
near Zhongli High School,

248
00:13:15,370 --> 00:13:16,370
I saw you walk out.

249
00:13:16,610 --> 00:13:17,490
With him.

250
00:13:22,080 --> 00:13:22,950
Wait a minute.

251
00:13:23,470 --> 00:13:26,330
You two went in and out
of the convenience store together?

252
00:13:26,330 --> 00:13:27,530
When did this happen?

253
00:13:29,950 --> 00:13:31,680
Since when are you two so close?

254
00:13:38,330 --> 00:13:39,030
We just...

255
00:13:39,510 --> 00:13:42,290
happened to bump into
each other at the convenience store.

256
00:13:42,290 --> 00:13:44,930
Yeah, I just helped the deadweight
think about

257
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:46,840
what his next part-time job should be.

258
00:13:46,840 --> 00:13:48,970
You're the deadweight, you...

259
00:13:49,200 --> 00:13:51,210
cockroach-fearing

260
00:13:51,240 --> 00:13:52,250
wimp.

261
00:13:53,580 --> 00:13:55,980
I'm a muscle man.
What do you mean by "wimp"?

262
00:13:55,980 --> 00:13:57,020
Wimp.

263
00:13:57,040 --> 00:13:58,560
Muscle Man eats the cake.

264
00:13:58,590 --> 00:14:00,780
-Muscle Man eats the cake.
-Eat the cake.

265
00:14:00,780 --> 00:14:01,860
Wimp.

266
00:14:02,760 --> 00:14:05,880
Say I'm afraid of cockroaches
one more time, I dare you.

267
00:14:21,230 --> 00:14:22,290
What are you doing?

268
00:14:23,890 --> 00:14:25,190
None of your business.

269
00:14:27,070 --> 00:14:28,200
You bought the bait?

270
00:14:29,930 --> 00:14:30,800
Yeah.

271
00:14:31,080 --> 00:14:33,080
I already put it next to the fridge.

272
00:14:36,060 --> 00:14:37,020
Thanks.

273
00:14:37,050 --> 00:14:38,440
You're welcome.

274
00:14:40,530 --> 00:14:41,460
That's it?

275
00:14:43,530 --> 00:14:44,420
Yeah.

276
00:14:45,360 --> 00:14:47,090
